WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.068
ROLLUP creates hierarchical subtotals In this
example the hierarchy

00:00:06.095 --> 00:00:11.789
is category then product followed by a grand total
Before running

00:00:11.815 --> 00:00:16.012
the query predict the types of rows you expect
product-level detail within

00:00:16.039 --> 00:00:21.820
each category a category subtotal and one final
total Run

00:00:21.846 --> 00:00:26.744
the query and inspect where grouped columns become
NULL Those NULL values

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:29.520
may indicate that the column has been rolled up to a
higher

00:00:29.546 --> 00:00:34.976
summary level Do not interpret every NULL in a
subtotal report as

00:00:34.989 --> 00:00:39.978
missing source data In advanced grouping output NULL
can be a structural

00:00:39.991 --> 00:00:45.194
placeholder This is why later we will use GROUPING
to distinguish a

00:00:45.221 --> 00:00:48.484
subtotal placeholder from a real NULL value in the
source
